export const mbaFaqs = [
  { q: "What is the difference between Placement Foundations and ConsultPro?", a: "Placement Foundations is the core interview preparation program for MBA placements across consulting, strategy, growth, category management, general management, operations, analytics, product, and other business roles. It covers structured problem solving, behavioural and HR interviews, business thinking, interview preparation strategy, and also includes two complimentary EdgeX GD Labs sessions for practical group discussion experience.\n\nConsultPro is a specialized program designed for students targeting consulting and strategy roles. It focuses on case interviews, guesstimates, consulting frameworks, structured thinking, executive communication, and rigorous case interview preparation.\n\nStudents targeting consulting firms are encouraged to consider the Placement Foundations + ConsultPro Combo, which combines both programs into one comprehensive preparation pathway while eliminating overlapping content." },
  { q: "I am targeting consulting. Should I only purchase ConsultPro?", a: "ConsultPro is designed specifically for students preparing for consulting and strategy interviews. If consulting is your primary and only target role, ConsultPro provides comprehensive preparation covering case interviews, guesstimates, consulting frameworks, structured thinking, and consulting-specific interview skills.\n\nHowever, if you also intend to participate in placements for other business roles alongside consulting, we recommend the Placement Foundations + ConsultPro Combo. In addition to consulting preparation, Placement Foundations develops transferable interview skills including behavioural interviews, HR interviews, business judgement, and interview strategy that are valuable across a wide range of MBA placement interviews." },
  { q: "I am not targeting consulting. Is Placement Foundations sufficient?", a: "Yes. Placement Foundations has been designed as a role-agnostic interview preparation program and is relevant for MBA students targeting consulting, strategy, growth & category management, general management, operations, analytics, product, and other business roles. The concepts taught are transferable across a wide range of placement interviews.\n\nThe course develops industry-agnostic and role-agnostic interview skills, including structured problem solving, behavioural interviews, business judgement, communication, and interview strategy, while using practical examples drawn from multiple business functions.\n\nHowever, for specialized roles such as Marketing, Finance, Product, or Analytics, students should continue preparing the relevant domain knowledge separately through their MBA coursework and other learning resources. We recommend using Placement Foundations alongside your core subject preparation to maximize your interview readiness." },
  { q: "Why are these courses designed around interview skills rather than specific companies?", a: "While every recruiter has its own interview process, the underlying skills they assess are remarkably consistent- structured thinking, business judgement, communication, problem-solving, and professionalism. EdgeX focuses on developing these transferable skills, enabling students to perform confidently across various business fucntions and industries." },
  { q: "Why should I choose EdgeX instead of preparing through YouTube, AI tools or Casebooks?", a: "YouTube videos, AI tools and Casebooks are excellent resources for learning individual concepts and practicing cases. However, successful interview preparation requires much more than isolated resources. EdgeX combines a structured curriculum with interviewer perspectives, guided case demonstrations, curated casebooks and learning resources, behavioural interview preparation, interview strategy, practical business examples, and live practice opportunities- bringing everything required for placement preparation together in one place." },
  { q: "How is the curriculum of courses designed?", a: "EdgeX courses have been developed by combining practical industry experience, interviewer insights, structured interview preparation methodologies, and real placement preparation experience. Rather than compiling isolated interview tips, the curriculum has been designed as a progressive learning journey that builds concepts systematically. Throughout the development process, experienced recruiters, industry professionals, and external advisors were consulted to help validate the breadth and completeness of the curriculum." },
  { q: "Will I receive access to future curriculum updates?", a: "Absolutely. Your enrollment includes access to all future updates made to your purchased course at no additional cost. Whether we introduce new lectures, expand practice material, refine existing modules, or incorporate insights from recruiters and recent placement cycles, you'll automatically receive access to the updated content. Our goal is to continuously improve the curriculum so that it remains relevant, comprehensive, and aligned with evolving recruitment practices." }
];

